ch.\",\n      \"Checked the right and wrong blanks listed in each choice explanation against the table. (1): (ウ) and (オ) wrong. (2): (ア), (イ), (エ) wrong. (3): (ア) and (オ) wrong. (5): (イ), (ウ), (エ) wrong. All are correct.\",\n      \"(ウ): the zero-sequence current in the faulted feeder flows opposite to the current in the healthy feeders. The explanation of this is technically correct.\",\n      \"reviewedFromPage [12] is consistent with T2-D 012.\"\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    \"unitKey\": \"20250323-power-q10\",\n    \"questionNumber\": 10,\n    \"part\": null,\n    \"status\": \"PASS\",\n    \"textIssues\": [],\n    \"choiceIssues\": [],\n    \"answerIssues\": [],\n    \"explanationIssues\": [],\n    \"figureIssues\": [],\n    \"sourceIssues\": [],\n    \"verifiedEvidence\": [\n      \"Checked against the official problem image (page footer -10- / T2-D 013). Voltage 6.6 kV, frequency 60 Hz, line length 2 km, three-phase three-wire underground line, 0.5 μF/km per core, unit [kV·A]. Choices: 5.5 / 8.2 / 16.4 / 28.4 / 49.3. All match. The only difference is that the original's full-width commas are written as '、', which is just formatting.\",\n      \"Recalculated the answer: C = 0.5 × 2 = 1 μF. Q = ωCV² = 2π×60 × 1×10⁻⁶ × (6.6×10³)² = 376.99 × 43.56 ≈ 16,421.7 V·A ≈ 16.4 kV·A. This matches the official answer (3).\",\n      \"Checked where each wrong choice comes from. (1) 16.42/3 ≈ 5.47 is the single-phase value ωCE². (2) Using the capacitance for 1 km: ω × 0.5 μF × V² ≈ 8.21. (4) 16.42 × √3 ≈ 28.44. (5) 3ωCV² ≈ 49.27. Each choice explanation's numbers and reasoning agree with these.\",\n      \"The official answer is 3, and the candidate's officialAnswer is 3. They match. No figure. reviewedFromPage [13] is consistent with T2-D 013.\",\n      \"The explanation makes no claim that depends on an outside source, so the empty officialReferenceUrls causes no problem.\"\n    ]\n  }\n]\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage"